WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:07.080
I thought we could do
an experiment here today.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:12.200
I asked you if we could try it
and see what happens.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:17.000
I'm quite fascinated by
the Saga Norén character.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:21.720
I don't think she knows,
but many believe she's got Asperger's.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:27.000
If I understand it correctly,
it makes her quite direct.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:31.400
For instance,
she doesn't understand irony.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.360
There are these sides to her.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.040
It seems like
it's easy for you to become her.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:43.160
-So I thought, what if she had my job?
-Yes...

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:48.120
Do you understand? What if there was
a Saga Norén talk show?

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:52.680
Yes... Okay.
She's been fired from her police job.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:58.000
She's trying to make a living
as a talk show host.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.000
Many are impressed that she managed
to get a job as a police officer.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:08.680
-So am I.
-She could have got this job as well.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:13.480
-Yes... She's not scared to ask.
-Let's give it a go.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:18.200
There's your notepad.
I don't know what you are going to ask.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.400
-But I will answer.
-Yes. Okay.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:25.280
Now you can introduce
the Saga Norén show.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:32.120
Hello! Today we will interview
this person. His name is Skavlan.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:45.320
-How many kids do you have?
-I've got four, soon five.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.920
Why do you have so many kids?

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:55.240
I'm scared of being alone, I guess.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:02:01.560
-Why are you scared of that?
-Well, I'm not. I can be alone.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:07.720
But I like having kids around me.
I like kids. I love kids.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:12.880
How many have you slept with?

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:23.160
That's a very personal question.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:27.120
-Why?
-It's a private matter.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:34.240
I have to draw a line where...
You can be personal, but not private.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:39.560
I know exactly how many there are.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.920
Counting them is easy,
but I won't do that here.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:47.000
-You know how many, but...?
-I don't want to say it.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:51.120
-You have a talk show.
-Yes.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.160
What's the purpose of it?

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:04.040
The idea is to create
good conversations.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:10.280
-What does that do?
-It will enlighten and entertain people.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:14.200
-So it's informative?
-Yes, that too.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.120
Why do you think
that you get to be on TV?

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:23.560
That's a very good question.
I've asked myself the same thing.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:29.440
Right now I'm thinking Saga Norén
should have had that job instead.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:33.880
I think you have
a narcissistic personality disorder.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:39.680
I... Then I would like to use
my power as the host to say...

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:43.160
-...thank you, Saga Norén.
-My pleasure.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:52.840
-She could have done it.
-Yes.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.040
It would have been an interesting show.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:59.960
Yes, you'd get to know quite a lot.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:03.200
Absolutely. I would have kept up.

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:06.560
Sofia, it's great to have you here.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:10.120
You can stay with us
a little bit longer.

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:14.040
I want you to listen to
an exciting story we're going to tell.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.560
Thank you, Sofia Helin.

